<title>BELGIUM: EU Commission to clear TAP airline aid - EU official.</title>
<headline>EU Commission to clear TAP airline aid - EU official.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission is due on Wednesday to clear the final 40-billion-escudo tranche of government aid to TAP Air Portugal, a senior Commission official told Reuters on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;On the basis of the report we have just received, they are on course so the Commission will authorise the payment,&quot; the official said.  </p>
<p>The aid payment is part of a package worth 180 billion escudos to the Portuguese state airline, which the Commission originally cleared in July 1994.</p>
<p>Portuguese Public Works Minister Joao Cravinho told reporters last September the airline would have to complete its restructuring plan before any talk of strategic alliances with other airlines.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800 (PIC)</p>
